To build a basic monostable (one‑shot) circuit with the TI NE555D (SOIC‑8) you will need the following schematic symbols.  
All of them are available in the standard KiCad libraries that ship with the “Timer” and “Device” libraries.  
Even though some parts (resistors, capacitors, power supply, ground) are very common, they still count as “related symbols” because they are required to complete the circuit.

| Symbol | Library | Typical use in the monostable circuit |
|--------|---------|---------------------------------------|
| **NE555D** | Timer | The core timer IC. |
| **V** | Device | DC voltage source (e.g., 5 V). |
| **GND** | Device | Ground reference. |
| **R** | Device | Timing resistor(s) and pull‑up resistor for the trigger input. |
| **C** | Device | Timing capacitor and any decoupling capacitor. |
| **LED** | Device | Indicator that lights when the output is high. |
| **SW_PUSH** | Device | Push‑button to generate the trigger pulse. |
| **Battery** | Device | Optional alternative to the V source (if you prefer a battery symbol). |

These symbols cover everything you need to draw a functional monostable NE555 circuit: power, ground, the timer IC, the trigger mechanism, the timing network (R & C), and an output indicator (LED). No other components are strictly required for a minimal example.

---

